[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-78680"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070244/assets/14d1fc5a92c28cc7f84c1ec23929701f1aca67b1a15d6113fa83f1428354fc11.png)\n\nConsider the ellipse centered at $(3,-1)$ with horizontal radius $2$ and vertical radius $3,$ as shown above. Which of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ),$  traverse the ellipse once in the counterclockwise direction starting at the point $A(5,-1)?$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-79273/selection/86fccb8a2558dfd94df3a1084c1ff7b56dcdc7863a9b732fdab0e683ee8a04a7" :answer/id #uuid "4cb54a88-8eb5-5849-a2ec-91249798d06c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\theta \\in [-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79273/selection/869e92fa37d662618b5776b5688120805f6a4ef64944d68a09668a86e88acb88" :answer/id #uuid "46b9267c-93a3-503b-a07f-904d0aa1048a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\theta \\in [\\pi ,\\frac{3\\pi }{2}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79273/selection/42113895f4a3b82bea25716b9e3a345a8aece1d1f1e571b15045782992436230" :answer/id #uuid "348d0679-80cc-51a3-844c-3795fddf01c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\theta \\in [\\pi ,2\\pi ]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79273/selection/254f7dc7c93945f5d800c08002268b921573aada24b982a69940059f541d28cc" :answer/id #uuid "d083840a-941f-529b-92bc-a21417ee64af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\theta \\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79273/selection/4205b99be199dc7950356b855ff4a5477c48c73878a7b026d25c035dbf46acb5" :answer/id #uuid "68d6142e-0b01-5ece-8ab8-4e0cd772b887" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\theta \\in [0,\\pi ]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79273/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3990cf93-b107-596e-989a-e69158aa996d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-79273/selection/4205b99be199dc7950356b855ff4a5477c48c73878a7b026d25c035dbf46acb5" :answer-field/choices ["q-79273/selection/86fccb8a2558dfd94df3a1084c1ff7b56dcdc7863a9b732fdab0e683ee8a04a7" "q-79273/selection/869e92fa37d662618b5776b5688120805f6a4ef64944d68a09668a86e88acb88" "q-79273/selection/42113895f4a3b82bea25716b9e3a345a8aece1d1f1e571b15045782992436230" "q-79273/selection/254f7dc7c93945f5d800c08002268b921573aada24b982a69940059f541d28cc" "q-79273/selection/4205b99be199dc7950356b855ff4a5477c48c73878a7b026d25c035dbf46acb5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-79273" :question/id #uuid "b9d06d5a-1710-506f-9441-28c4dc1ef4cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-79273" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070244/assets/48c5190fc4f45f4bf3e76a56977339559ceb30ca90a41411d3bc4df2362b0787.png)\n\nThe semi-ellipse above is defined by the parametric equations \n\n$$\nx=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nWhat is the domain of the parameter $\\theta ?$" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ are\n\n$$\nx=a\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=b\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=4$ and $b=3.$ Therefore, the parametric equations of the *full* ellipse are\n\n$$\nx=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nTo restrict the parameterization to a semi-ellipse, we associate the parameter $\\theta $ with the central angle formed by a point $(x,y)$ on the elipse and the $x$-axis. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070244/assets/546b9f72124a7eb05877db3600e40b5772404a1a3378de67cfbe3320c78ac2ba.png)\n\nWe can see that if we restrict $\\theta $ to $[0,\\pi ]$, we get the semi-ellipse.\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the semi-ellipse are \n\n$$\nx=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,\\pi ].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-79273/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b51a7bc-7701-539f-9e20-dfc7f2574559"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-79273"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-79287/selection/6a1c494bca4e9149ca771eb02216f2563453ed35e44ff5cfc14058db900c9346" :answer/id #uuid "9c04c4a0-2411-5cd3-a749-0d949b6aed42" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +3,\\,y=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79287/selection/9ff91a0dc580f4c6059b643bb5fbf964c39a5e9da5fba6a8337cf70fc43fd32b" :answer/id #uuid "7a077b25-808c-5e1f-8296-4b190dd6f6db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +3,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79287/selection/732d03cbe9a3ab1c6d12178b693cc75a2a937e507d5598a862c439e7c31346eb" :answer/id #uuid "0d3a4619-1ca2-528b-920a-f4767aa1db0b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -3,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79287/selection/5f2850578c1f396e1b1205414b5ecea85bd1143adb219804213640522ae9c5a7" :answer/id #uuid "63d32c88-76e2-5390-82c6-9eb900a34c1a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=9\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -2,\\,y=25\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79287/selection/a4b91f7b955a578f9565c4b496d7c2795be1a80a152b6eb044b5222eb4ae324c" :answer/id #uuid "13435a9e-8fec-5dbb-add7-b89405f650a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +2,\\,y=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79287/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f735d59c-2e8a-5e2f-bfbe-439b61b0d80d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-79287/selection/6a1c494bca4e9149ca771eb02216f2563453ed35e44ff5cfc14058db900c9346" :answer-field/choices ["q-79287/selection/6a1c494bca4e9149ca771eb02216f2563453ed35e44ff5cfc14058db900c9346" "q-79287/selection/9ff91a0dc580f4c6059b643bb5fbf964c39a5e9da5fba6a8337cf70fc43fd32b" "q-79287/selection/732d03cbe9a3ab1c6d12178b693cc75a2a937e507d5598a862c439e7c31346eb" "q-79287/selection/5f2850578c1f396e1b1205414b5ecea85bd1143adb219804213640522ae9c5a7" "q-79287/selection/a4b91f7b955a578f9565c4b496d7c2795be1a80a152b6eb044b5222eb4ae324c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-79287" :question/id #uuid "9082f86b-7c0f-5dd7-b074-5c0e7d067128" :question/math-academy-id "q-79287" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070244/assets/07ec13485a828c8f5cd99ae2fbc3f7444135ba3c1cdf790762edb01b9726317e.png)\n\nWhich of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ),$ generate the ellipse shown above?" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of an ellipse centered at the point $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ are\n\n$$\nx=a\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +h,\\,y=b\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +k,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, the ellipse is centered at the point $(3,2),$ $a=3$ and $b=5.$ Therefore, the parametric equations of the ellipse are\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +3,\\,y=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-79287/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6d82541c-40ca-5df9-aa17-c20b201fadd4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-79287"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-79377/selection/8414c773ffebe64725a213548b241f2072397fce5102f518db5286bbf209a5a2" :answer/id #uuid "1c46b20b-d7fa-5576-ae03-0355b8965214" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(x+5)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{18}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79377/selection/9e2554b28d08bea09623bed09db803640c5db5dc3551b7f37d1e78b53748f77b" :answer/id #uuid "5869fe13-1f93-5842-b33f-b20908c60d47" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{3}+\\frac{(y-5)^{2}}{6}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79377/selection/3512508d3a3c95cc39f90d972f0a7c84dbe187f939b03c4b28e5f1a763d029bb" :answer/id #uuid "5c0d8db5-38cc-5572-a53a-4584905f8b95" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(x+5)^{2}}{6}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{36}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79377/selection/79529b584818195aac904f8be398d68e8dba8f7d0ab26b2dbf10bc1365a7d15a" :answer/id #uuid "a88347c4-eb37-5e1b-ba92-52d2e2b28c19" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{36}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79377/selection/99e3cf5fd2015ea90da63ee477899c629bc4aa6209559f178885ad6549456b3c" :answer/id #uuid "e7ce2998-0398-5a1e-92b2-b2d83a4c7a53" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(x+5)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{36}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79377/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "daebd331-accc-5e35-b808-aeaa31338f43" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-79377/selection/99e3cf5fd2015ea90da63ee477899c629bc4aa6209559f178885ad6549456b3c" :answer-field/choices ["q-79377/selection/8414c773ffebe64725a213548b241f2072397fce5102f518db5286bbf209a5a2" "q-79377/selection/9e2554b28d08bea09623bed09db803640c5db5dc3551b7f37d1e78b53748f77b" "q-79377/selection/3512508d3a3c95cc39f90d972f0a7c84dbe187f939b03c4b28e5f1a763d029bb" "q-79377/selection/79529b584818195aac904f8be398d68e8dba8f7d0ab26b2dbf10bc1365a7d15a" "q-79377/selection/99e3cf5fd2015ea90da63ee477899c629bc4aa6209559f178885ad6549456b3c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-79377" :question/id #uuid "7905e0ad-e4b9-544c-af54-d96f3b36bc86" :question/math-academy-id "q-79377" :question/problem "Determine the Cartesian equation of the ellipse\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -5,\\,y=6\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -2,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi .\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find the Cartesian equation of the ellipse, we need to eliminate the parameter $\\theta .$ We can do this using the Pythagorean theorem.\n\nBy isolating the $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ term in the $x$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -5 \\\\ \\frac{x+5}{3} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{(x+5)^{2}}{{3}^{2}} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{(x+5)^{2}}{9} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta ,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy isolating the $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =6\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -2 \\\\ \\frac{y+2}{6} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{{6}^{2}} & ={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{36} & ={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nAdding the two equations and using ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x+5)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{36} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the Cartesian equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x+5)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{36}=1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-79377/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6e75170b-1e28-52c1-b0ab-f50ffde6c262"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-79377"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
